Package: immunerepertoire
Type: Package
Title: Shared Core for Reproducible Immune Repertoire and Single-Cell Analysis
Version: 0.2.0
Authors@R:
    person("Zineb", "Sbihi",
           email = "ZinebSBIHI@users.noreply.github.com",
           role = c("aut", "cre"),
           comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0002-6695-7695"))
Description: The shared functions behind three companion analysis pipelines
    for adaptive immune receptor repertoires (bulk and single-cell, T-cell and
    B-cell receptors) and single-cell gene expression. It provides clonotype
    definition and collapsing, diversity and clonality indices, rarefaction to
    a common sequencing depth, repertoire overlap, gene usage, differential
    clonal abundance against a within-subject baseline with descriptive
    category and statistical significance kept as separate axes, convergence
    between subjects tested against a label-permutation null, paired
    comparisons that report the smallest p-value attainable at small sample
    size, and B-cell receptor processing (one heavy chain per cell, clonal
    inference, germlines, somatic hypermutation, isotypes). Every analysis is
    driven by a single validated configuration file, and every run writes the
    resolved configuration and session information beside its outputs.
